-- title:
--   Avg Over Distinct Bounded Le Avg Over Uniform Add Tv Of Any K
-- statement:
--   **A bounded average over distinct tuples is controlled by the uniform average.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let $k\in\mathbb{N}$, and let $F:\mathbb{F}_q^k\to\mathbb{R}$ satisfy $0\le F(x)\le1$. If $\mathcal D_{\ne}$ is uniform on injective tuples and $\mathcal U$ is uniform on all tuples, then
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal D_{\ne}}F(x)\le\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal U}F(x)+\operatorname{TV}(\mathcal U,\mathcal D_{\ne}).
--   $$
--
--   The statement remains valid when the injective support is empty. It is the bounded-test-function comparison used to replace distinct-height averaging by uniform averaging.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.avgOver_distinct_bounded_le_avgOver_uniform_add_tv_of_any_k`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
